-## Iteration N - Story: US-872 WhatsApp interactive list message for menu category browsing
-
-### What was implemented
-- Added `MENU_BROWSE` intent to `src/assistant/data/routing.json` with action `menu_browse`
-- Added `menu_browse` case to `dispatchAction` switch in `src/assistant/pipeline/stages/action-dispatch.ts`
-- Implemented `handleMenuBrowse()` function that:
-  - Restricts to `makan-moments` profile only (hostel falls back to LLM response)
-  - Fetches menu items via `fetchMenuItems()` from `src/tools/fnb-menu.ts`
-  - Groups items by category, picks top 3 categories × top 3 items = 9 rows (within WhatsApp 10-row limit)
-  - Builds interactive list payload using `buildListMessage()` with `state.interactivePayload`
-  - Webchat fallback: phone starts with `webchat-` → plain text with `*Category*` headers
-  - Row IDs use `item_<code>` format for deterministic cart operations
-  - Text fallback if `buildListMessage` fails or interactive is disabled
-- Updated `config-integration.integration.test.ts` validActions list to include `flow` and `menu_browse`
-- Added 13-test file: `src/assistant/__tests__/menu-browse-list.test.ts` covering all acceptance criteria
-- Build: esbuild passes (3 pre-existing warnings, 0 errors)
-- Tests: 887/894 pass (7 pre-existing failures, down from 9 before this story)
-
-### Patterns discovered
-- `handleLLMReply` has special-case checks for specific intents (MENU_FILTER_PRICE, MENU_SPECIALS) — new distinct handlers need their own `case` in `dispatchAction` switch
-- Webchat detection: `phone.startsWith('webchat-')` pattern used throughout codebase
-- Interactive payload: set `state.interactivePayload` in action-dispatch; `response-processor.ts` sends it via `sendWhatsAppInteractiveMessage`
-- `buildListMessage` enforces 10 TOTAL rows across all sections (not 10 per section)
-- `fetchMenuItems()` parses MCP response in multiple formats (array, {items:[]}, {data:[]}, text)
-
-### Gotchas
-- `config-integration.integration.test.ts` validates all routing.json actions against a hardcoded list — must add new actions to `validActions` array when adding new routing action types
-- `prd.json` uses UTF-8 with special chars — always open with `encoding='utf-8'` in Python
-- WhatsApp row title max is 24 chars — truncate long item names with `…`
