-### What was implemented
-- Added `TIER_EVALUATION_CYCLE_HOURS = 6` constant (exported) to messaging-limits.ts reflecting Meta's Oct 7 2025 change from 24-48h to 6h evaluation cycle
-- Updated GET /analytics/messaging-limits response to include `portfolioMessagingLimit` field (same value as `tier`) for explicit portfolio-level naming per US-910 AC#1
-- Added `tierEvaluationCycleHours: 6` field to API response per AC#4
-- Both DB-unavailable fallback and normal response paths updated
-- Added 5 new Vitest tests in US-910 describe block:
-  - TIER_EVALUATION_CYCLE_HOURS is 6
-  - Second phone number inherits portfolio tier (not baseline 1K)
-  - All portfolio phone numbers resolve to same limit
-  - Tier upgrade affects all numbers simultaneously
-  - No 1000-message baseline tier exists
-### Patterns discovered
-- The existing code already used portfolio-level semantics (single DB key `rainbow_portfolio_tier`) — the story primarily required making this explicit in the API surface and adding the 6h evaluation cycle
-- Double-export error: `export const X` + `export { X }` causes esbuild transform error; remove from re-export list when using inline export
-### Gotchas
-- prd.json needs utf-8 encoding flag for Python json.load on Windows (UnicodeDecodeError with default cp1252)
