-## Iteration [Ralph] - Story: US-897 AI waiter returning-customer order history
-### What was implemented
-- **New file: `src/assistant/order-history-store.ts`**: Persists completed webchat order items to `webchat_order_history` table (raw pg, auto-created on startup). Provides `saveOrderHistory()` and `getLastOrder()` functions.
-- **`src/tools/cart.ts`**: Added `saveOrderHistory` import and fire-and-forget call in `order_confirm_submit` handler after order is placed, before cart is cleared.
-- **`src/routes/public/webchat-api.ts`**: 
-  - Modified `GET /:profileId/greeting` to check for returning customer's last order (makan-moments only). Returns `lastOrder` field with available items, omitted out-of-stock items, and a "Welcome back! Order your usual again?" greeting.
-  - Added `POST /:profileId/reorder` endpoint that populates the session cart with items from the last completed order, checking menu availability and omitting out-of-stock items.
-- **Admin toggle**: Feature checks `settings.repeatOrderEnabled` (defaults to `true`/enabled). Can be disabled via admin settings.
-- **Tests**: 5 Vitest tests in `src/assistant/__tests__/order-history.test.ts` covering first-time empty lookup, returning-session correct cart, save persistence, and DB error graceful handling.
-### Patterns discovered
-- The DB pool mock must have a default `.mockResolvedValue()` because the module runs startup migration queries at import time (CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS)
-- Cart items are in-memory and cleared after checkout — persistent order history requires a separate DB table
-- The `fetchMenuItems()` returns `DisambiguationCandidate[]` with `code` and `available` fields, suitable for availability checking
-### Gotchas
-- The `saveOrderHistory` function signature was enriched by linter to take an object param with phone, tableInfo, totalAmount — the cart.ts call needed to match
-- The linter also added order stage transition (ORDERING) to the reorder endpoint for consistency with cart population
-
-
-## Iteration [Ralph] - Story: US-897 AI waiter returning-customer order history
-### What was implemented
-- **Drizzle schema**: Added `webchat_order_history` table in `shared/schema-tables.ts` with session_id, phone, profile_id, items_json, table_info_json, order_id, total_amount, created_at
-- **Order history store** (`src/assistant/order-history-store.ts`): Updated to match new Drizzle schema with `saveOrderHistory()` (object params) and `getLastOrder()` returning items, tableInfo, orderId, totalAmount, placedAt
-- **Cart order persistence** (`src/tools/cart.ts`): `order_confirm_submit` handler saves completed order snapshot via `saveOrderHistory()` with profileId and customerJid from closure
-- **Greeting endpoint** (`src/routes/public/webchat-api.ts`): Enhanced `GET /:profileId/greeting` to detect returning customers, check menu availability (via `fetchMenuItems()`), omit out-of-stock items, and return `lastOrder` data with "Welcome back!" greeting
-- **Reorder endpoint** (`POST /:profileId/reorder`): Populates cart with available items from last order, transitions to ORDERING stage, omits out-of-stock items with notification
-- **Admin toggle**: Feature controlled by `settings.repeatOrderEnabled` (default: enabled) per AC#4
-- **5 Vitest tests**: first-time session returns null, returning session returns correct cart, save persists correctly, DB error graceful handling for both save and get
-### Patterns discovered
-- Spiral worker had already implemented most of the endpoint code — Ralph validated, fixed schema alignment, and ensured order stage transition on reorder
-- prd.json was truncated (only 3KB vs 202KB backup) — restored from prd.json.bak before marking story
-### Status
-Build passes. 5/5 tests pass. Story marked passes=true.
