-## Iteration [Ralph] - Story: US-897 AI waiter returning-customer order history
-### What was implemented
-- **Server-side was already complete** from prior spiral work:
-  - `src/assistant/order-history-store.ts`: DB table `webchat_order_history`, `saveOrderHistory()` (fire-and-forget on order completion), `getLastOrder()` (latest order per session)
-  - `src/routes/public/webchat-api.ts` greeting endpoint: returns `lastOrder` data with out-of-stock filtering via menu availability check
-  - `src/routes/public/webchat-api.ts` reorder endpoint (`POST /reorder`): populates cart from last order, filters unavailable items
-  - `src/tools/cart.ts`: calls `saveOrderHistory()` on order submission
-  - `src/assistant/__tests__/order-history.test.ts`: 5 tests (first-time null, returning cart, save, DB error handling)
-- **Added client-side webchat changes** (`src/public/webchat.html`):
-  - CSS: `.quick-reply-container` and `.quick-reply-btn` styles (pill button, hover/disabled states)
-  - `appendQuickReplyButton()`: renders a quick-reply button below the greeting message
-  - `handleReorder()`: calls `POST /reorder`, shows cart confirmation with item list, handles errors
-  - `initHistory()` updated: new/empty sessions now call `/greeting` endpoint instead of using static `profile.greeting`, enabling server to return `lastOrder` data; shows "Order the same again" button when `lastOrder` is present
-- **Added `repeatOrderEnabled` toggle** to `settings.json` (default true)
-
-### Patterns discovered
-- The greeting endpoint was already wired up server-side but the webchat client never called it — it used the static `profile.greeting` from `window.__WEBCHAT_PROFILE__`
-- Quick-reply buttons use `messagesEl.insertBefore(container, typingEl)` pattern, same as message bubbles
-
-### Gotchas
-- prd.json requires utf-8-sig encoding for Python json.load on Windows (BOM prefix)
-- Linter/hooks may revert file changes — need to re-apply edits if hooks modify files
-
-### Status
-Build passes. 5 tests pass. Story marked passes=true.
